<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light">
  <title>${project_name_short} &ndash; Read Me First</title>
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="manual/assets/favicon.png">
  <style>
    /* The fnTech3 flame: orange #fc5c00 on black, with the banner's ember red.
       The same colours as the Player Guide in manual/. */
    :root {
      --bg: #0b0806;
      --surface: #15100c;
      --surface-2: #1d1510;
      --line: #34261c;
      --line-strong: #4b3627;
      --text: #f7efe8;
      --text-soft: #dccdc1;
      --muted: #b29f90;
      --accent: #fc5c00;
      --accent-strong: #ff8038;
      --accent-ink: #160800;
      --accent-soft: rgba(252, 92, 0, 0.14);
      --accent-line: rgba(252, 92, 0, 0.5);
      --ember: #e02000;
      --code-bg: rgba(252, 92, 0, 0.13);
      --code-text: #ffc7a1;
      --glow-1: rgba(252, 92, 0, 0.18);
      --glow-2: rgba(224, 32, 0, 0.11);
      --shadow: 0 18px 44px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
      --font: "Segoe UI Variable Text", "Segoe UI", system-ui, -apple-system, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
      --font-display: "Segoe UI Variable Display", "Segoe UI", system-ui, -apple-system, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
      --mono: "Cascadia Code", "Cascadia Mono", Consolas, "SFMono-Regular", Menlo, monospace;
    }

    @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
      :root {
        --bg: #fdf8f4;
        --surface: #ffffff;
        --surface-2: #fff3ea;
        --line: #f0dccd;
        --line-strong: #e2c2aa;
        --text: #1d130c;
        --text-soft: #3d2c20;
        --muted: #6f5848;
        --accent-strong: #b53e00;
        --accent-ink: #1a0900;
        --accent-soft: rgba(252, 92, 0, 0.1);
        --accent-line: rgba(181, 62, 0, 0.45);
        --code-bg: #fff0e4;
        --code-text: #a33900;
        --glow-1: rgba(252, 92, 0, 0.12);
        --glow-2: rgba(224, 32, 0, 0.06);
        --shadow: 0 18px 40px rgba(94, 45, 10, 0.14);
      }
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      background:
        radial-gradient(60rem 30rem at 10% -6rem, var(--glow-1), transparent 70%),
        radial-gradient(48rem 26rem at 95% -8rem, var(--glow-2), transparent 70%),
        var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font: 16px/1.68 var(--font);
    }

    main {
      width: min(1060px, calc(100% - 32px));
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 40px 0 56px;
    }

    a {
      color: var(--accent-strong);
      text-decoration-color: var(--accent-line);
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }

    a:hover {
      text-decoration-color: currentColor;
    }

    a:focus-visible {
      outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
      outline-offset: 2px;
    }

    code {
      padding: 0.12em 0.42em;
      border-radius: 6px;
      background: var(--code-bg);
      color: var(--code-text);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.87em;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    .hero,
    .section {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 24px;
      background: var(--surface);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .hero {
      position: relative;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 36px;
      padding: 42px 44px;
      overflow: hidden;
      background:
        radial-gradient(120% 150% at 0% 0%, rgba(252, 92, 0, 0.3), transparent 55%),
        radial-gradient(90% 130% at 100% 0%, rgba(224, 32, 0, 0.22), transparent 60%),
        var(--surface);
    }

    .hero-logo {
      width: 150px;
      height: 150px;
      flex: none;
      filter: drop-shadow(0 12px 30px rgba(252, 92, 0, 0.45));
    }

    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      color: var(--accent-strong);
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.15em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    h1,
    h2,
    h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      color: var(--text);
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 4.2rem);
      font-weight: 800;
      line-height: 1;
      letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    }

    .tagline {
      margin: 10px 0 0;
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 0.98rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .tagline::after {
      content: "";
      display: block;
      width: 76px;
      height: 4px;
      margin-top: 16px;
      border-radius: 4px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent), var(--ember));
    }

    .subtitle {
      max-width: 660px;
      margin: 16px 0 0;
      color: var(--text-soft);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }

    .buttons {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 26px;
    }

    .button {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      padding: 11px 22px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: transform 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease;
    }

    .button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-1px);
    }

    .button-primary {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff8a2e, var(--accent) 45%, #e8430a);
      box-shadow: 0 10px 26px rgba(252, 92, 0, 0.35);
      color: var(--accent-ink);
    }

    .button-secondary {
      border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
      background: var(--surface-2);
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .button-secondary:hover {
      border-color: var(--accent-line);
    }

    .stats,
    .feature-grid,
    .doc-grid,
    .steps {
      display: grid;
      gap: 14px;
    }

    .stats {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
      margin-top: 18px;
    }

    .card,
    .feature-group,
    .doc-column,
    .step {
      padding: 18px 20px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 16px;
      background: var(--surface-2);
    }

    .card strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 4px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .card p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--text);
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .section {
      margin-top: 22px;
      padding: 30px 32px;
    }

    h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 1.6rem;
      font-weight: 750;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    h2 span {
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    h3 {
      margin: 0 0 6px;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    .lead {
      max-width: 820px;
      margin: 10px 0 0;
      color: var(--text-soft);
    }

    .feature-grid,
    .doc-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
      margin-top: 20px;
    }

    .feature-group p,
    .step p,
    li {
      color: var(--text-soft);
    }

    .feature-group p,
    .step p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
      margin-top: 20px;
      counter-reset: step;
    }

    .step {
      position: relative;
      padding-top: 52px;
    }

    .step::before {
      counter-increment: step;
      content: counter(step);
      position: absolute;
      top: 16px;
      left: 20px;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      width: 28px;
      height: 28px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--ember));
      color: var(--accent-ink);
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .note {
      margin: 18px 0 0;
      padding: 14px 18px;
      border: 1px solid var(--accent-line);
      border-left-width: 4px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      color: var(--text-soft);
    }

    ul {
      margin: 10px 0 0;
      padding-left: 1.3em;
    }

    li {
      margin: 0.35em 0;
    }

    li::marker {
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    .footer {
      margin: 18px 0 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.93rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 720px) {
      main {
        width: calc(100% - 32px);
        padding-top: 18px;
      }

      .hero {
        flex-direction: column;
        padding: 28px 22px;
        text-align: center;
      }

      .hero-logo {
        width: 112px;
        height: 112px;
      }

      .tagline::after {
        margin-left: auto;
        margin-right: auto;
      }

      .buttons {
        justify-content: center;
      }

      .section {
        padding: 24px 20px;
        border-radius: 18px;
      }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html {
        scroll-behavior: auto;
      }

      .button {
        transition: none;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <img class="hero-logo" src="manual/assets/fntech3-256.png" width="150" height="150" alt="The ${project_name_short} flame">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Read me first &middot; version ${version}</p>
        <h1>${project_name_short}</h1>
        <p class="tagline">Unified source port for id Tech 3</p>
        <p class="subtitle"><strong>${project_name_short}</strong> is a free, modern engine for the classic games of the Quake III era: <em>Quake III Arena</em>, <em>Quake Live</em>, <em>Return to Castle Wolfenstein</em>, <em>Wolfenstein: Enemy Territory</em>, <em>Star Trek Voyager: Elite Force</em>, <em>Star Wars Jedi Knight: Jedi Academy</em>, <em>Star Wars Jedi Knight II: Jedi Outcast</em>, <em>American McGee's Alice</em>, <em>Heavy Metal: F.A.K.K.2</em> and <em>Medal of Honor: Allied Assault</em>. It plays the copies you already own, with sharper graphics, 3D sound and widescreen support.</p>
        <div class="buttons">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="manual/index.html">Open the Player Guide</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="#getting-started">Getting started</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="manual/games.html">The games</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="stats">
      <article class="card">
        <strong>Plays</strong>
        <p>${compatibility_target}</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <strong>Version</strong>
        <p>${version}</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <strong>Licence</strong>
        <p><a href="LICENSE">GPL version 2</a></p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="section" id="getting-started">
      <h2><span>1.</span> Getting Started</h2>
      <p class="lead">fnTech3 contains no game files. You need your own installed copy of a game; fnTech3 plays it without changing it.</p>
      <p class="note"><strong>Start with a clean game folder.</strong> We recommend running ${project_name_short} without other asset packages, or custom game code (QVMs), in the game's base folder, such as Quake III Arena's <code>baseq3</code>. They can replace files ${project_name_short} relies on and clash with its features. For example, the baseq3a package brings its own QVMs for Quake III Arena, which may interfere with ${project_name_short}'s widescreen correction. To keep using packages like these, turn the corrections off: <code>r_fovCorrection 0</code> for the view, <code>cl_hudAspect 0</code> for the HUD and <code>cl_menuAspect 0</code> for menus. The <a href="manual/widescreen.html#the-four-settings">Widescreen guide</a> explains each setting.</p>
      <div class="steps">
        <article class="step">
          <h3>Keep the files together</h3>
          <p>You have already unpacked this download into a folder. Keep everything in it beside <code>${executable_basename}.exe</code>: the engine looks there for <code>fntech3-pkg.fnz</code>, <code>fnql-web.pak</code>, its three renderer files and the libraries.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="step">
          <h3>Start your game</h3>
          <p>Open <code>${executable_basename}-launcher.exe</code>: it finds your games in Steam, GOG and the usual game folders and starts the one you click. You can also name the game, and its folder, in a shortcut: <code>+set com_gameProfile quake3 +set fs_basepath "&lt;your Quake III folder&gt;"</code>.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="step">
          <h3>Play, then tune</h3>
          <p>Press the key below <strong>Esc</strong> (or <strong>Shift+Esc</strong>) to open the console, where every setting can be changed. <strong>Alt+Enter</strong> switches between a window and fullscreen.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="note"><strong>Which games are available?</strong> Every build includes all sixteen game profiles. Quake III Arena and Quake Live are playable; other games remain experimental, with the limitations described in the <a href="manual/games.html">Games guide</a>. Quake Live's client and games with Windows-only retail modules need Windows. No development build or opt-in flag is required. Complete compatibility is not yet established for any game.</p>
      <p class="footer">The <a href="manual/getting-started.html">Getting Started guide</a> walks through shortcuts, the console, settings files and where your saves and screenshots go. Steam features in Quake Live need a separately supplied Steam add-on, which this download does not include; without it they say they are unavailable rather than pretending to work.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="features">
      <h2><span>2.</span> Features</h2>
      <p class="lead">What fnTech3 adds to the games it plays. Each guide says which games a feature works in; Quake Live's own menus, Steam and Workshop features belong to Quake Live alone.</p>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Unified game compatibility</h3>
          <p>One engine for many games. fnTech3 starts one game at a time and follows that game's own rules &ndash; its game code, online play, demos and saved games &ndash; so every game plays like itself.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>A launcher that finds your games</h3>
          <p>It looks in Steam, GOG, disc installs and the usual game folders, lists every installation with its icon, store and folder, and starts the one you click &ndash; in the mode and with the mod you choose.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Fast, modern hardware rendering</h3>
          <p>Three renderers in every game &ndash; GLx, Vulkan and RTX &ndash; built to make the most of today's graphics cards. RTX ray traces each map with light from its own lamps, sky and sun, including liquid reflections and water refraction tested on Quake III's q3dm12.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Modern visual upgrades</h3>
          <p>Optional HDR, smoother edges, sharper textures, glow, smooth lights with real shadows, lights for each map's own lamps, motion blur, lens flares, softer smoke, livelier water, an underwater view and atmospheric fog.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Improved player visibility</h3>
          <p>An optional glow and outline on other players in Quake III Arena and Quake Live, in team or enemy colours of your choice, and a cartoon cel-shaded look for every game.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Better modern hardware and OS support</h3>
          <p>High resolutions and refresh rates, borderless windows, instant Alt+Enter, controllers you can plug in at any time, and each game's own icon, remade in high resolution.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Low-latency, configurable controls</h3>
          <p>Raw mouse input, Quake Live's exact mouse sensitivity and acceleration, the classic mouse styles, gamepads, and typing in any language.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Modern spatial audio</h3>
          <p>3D sound: headphone surround, surround speakers, room echo, sounds muffled by walls and sound zones for the maps of seven games &ndash; with the original sound mixer still there if you want it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Major quality-of-life improvements</h3>
          <p>A console that scales, scrolls smoothly, suggests commands and copies and pastes; widescreen view and HUD for every game made for 4:3 screens; silence when you switch away; and less work for your computer in the background.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>In-game entity editor</h3>
          <p>Move, add, copy, delete and change a map's objects in the game, with undo, and save them as a <code>maps/&lt;map&gt;.ent</code> file that the server loads in place of the map's own &ndash; in every game.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Better screenshots, video and streaming tools</h3>
          <p>PNG, JPEG, TGA and BMP screenshots, copying to the clipboard, your own file names, camera notes, map previews, watermarks, cube maps, any resolution, and video recording through FFmpeg.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Faster content handling</h3>
          <p>Quicker starts and map changes with big collections of mods and maps, higher limits, fast downloads and, in Quake Live, the Workshop items a server needs, fetched for you.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Greater stability and security</h3>
          <p>Many fixes from Quake3e and FnQuake3, careful checking of every game file, demo and network message, less memory, better protection online, and graceful fallbacks when an optional feature is missing.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="documentation">
      <h2><span>3.</span> Documentation</h2>
      <p class="lead">The Player Guide in the <code>manual</code> folder covers everything, in plain language, and works offline in any web browser.</p>
      <div class="doc-grid">
        <article class="doc-column">
          <h3>Player guides</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="manual/getting-started.html">Getting started</a>: set up, start a game, use the console and settings.</li>
            <li><a href="manual/launcher.html">Launcher</a>: find the games on your computer and start one with a click.</li>
            <li><a href="manual/games.html">Games</a>: every game, what you need, playing online, and what works today.</li>
            <li><a href="manual/display.html">Graphics</a>: window and fullscreen, smoother edges, lighting, shadows, water, fog and glow.</li>
            <li><a href="manual/widescreen.html">Widescreen</a>: field of view, HUD, menus and movies on wide screens.</li>
            <li><a href="manual/player-highlights.html">Player highlights</a>: making other players stand out.</li>
            <li><a href="manual/audio.html">Sound</a>: headphones, surround, 3D sound and fixing sound problems.</li>
            <li><a href="manual/console.html">Console</a>: commands, suggestions, copy and paste, and its look.</li>
            <li><a href="manual/screenshots.html">Screenshots</a>: formats, names, watermarks, map previews and cube maps.</li>
            <li><a href="manual/glx.html">GLx renderer</a> and <a href="manual/rtx.html">RTX ray tracing</a>: the default renderer and the ray tracer.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="doc-column">
          <h3>For the technically minded</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="docs/fntech3/COMPATIBILITY.md">Compatibility ledger</a> (included): every game's test results and what is still open.</li>
            <li><a href="CHANGELOG.md">Changelog</a> (included): what changed in each release, and the <a href="docs/fntech3/RELEASING.md">release guide</a>.</li>
            <li><a href="docs/fnql/RTX_RENDERER.md">RTX Renderer Contract</a> (included): how the ray tracer works and its limits.</li>
            <li><a href="docs/fnql/TECHNICAL.md">Technical notes</a> (included): the engine's design, inherited from FnQL.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/fnTech3/blob/main/BUILD.md">Build guide</a>: compiling fnTech3, including the experimental games.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/fnTech3/blob/main/docs/fntech3/ARCHITECTURE.md">Architecture overview</a>: how the engine fits together.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/fnTech3/issues">Report a problem</a> on GitHub.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="credits">
      <h2><span>4.</span> Credits</h2>
      <p class="lead">${project_name_short} combines FnQuake3 and FnQL with the engine line of id Software, ioquake3 and Quake3e. QLSRP, OpenJK, OpenAlice, iortcw, Lilium Voyager and other projects helped document how the games behave, for work written independently for ${project_name_short}.</p>
      <p class="lead">Other compatibility and feature work draws on projects such as <a href="https://bitbucket.org/CPMADevs/cnq3">CNQ3</a>, <a href="https://github.com/zturtleman/spearmint">Spearmint</a>, <a href="https://github.com/brugal/wolfcamql">WolfcamQL</a>, Luigi Auriemma's <a href="https://aluigi.altervista.org/papers.htm#qldec">qldec</a> and <a href="https://github.com/Paril/DarkMatter-Q2">DarkMatter-Q2</a>.</p>
      <p class="footer">The full history, thanks and trademark notices are in <a href="CREDITS.md">CREDITS.md</a> and <a href="THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md">THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</a>. All game names and trademarks belong to their owners; fnTech3 is not made or endorsed by them.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
